#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Async transcription job runner with a REST upload endpoint and an MCP endpoint.

Meetings take minutes and Hermes' tools have a fixed deadline, so nothing here
blocks: a caller submits audio, gets a job id, and polls (or reads the result
later). One worker thread runs `meeting-transcribe` at a time. No inference is
managed here: the ASR is Unsloth Studio's transcribe workflow, audio.cpp (which
diarizes itself) or Mistral, all over HTTP.

The model id names its provider: unsloth.* goes to the studio, mistral.voxtral-*
to Mistral, anything else to audio.cpp.

    ./meeting-job --dir /mnt/cache/mcp-meeting-transcribe --token secret

    # upload (n8n: HTTP Request, binary body; curl:)
    curl --data-binary @meeting.m4a \
         "http://halogen-host:8099/jobs?filename=meeting.m4a&language=it" \
         -H "Authorization: Bearer secret"
    # -> {"id":"1a2b...","status":"queued"}

    curl -H "Authorization: Bearer secret" http://halogen-host:8099/jobs/1a2b...

    # the recorder announces a finished recording (idempotent; GET /hooks lists them)
    curl -d '{"day":"2026-10-20","recording":"12-35-09","files":["audio/a.mp3"]}' \
         http://halogen-host:8099/hook

    # Hermes MCP over HTTP (Streamable HTTP, JSON responses) at POST /mcp
    # tools: transcribe_meeting, meeting_status, meeting_result

MCP calls are stateless JSON-RPC 2.0: initialize, tools/list, tools/call, ping.
Large recordings should go through POST /jobs; the MCP tool takes base64 for
small ones. Auth is a bearer token on every route but /health. Stdlib only.
"""

